{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#950","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#950","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#950\",\"parent_revision\":\"07236daa34b81adb444a201c49569cf94b158992\",\"root_revision\":\"4c8c16801c7a08b99e20269581253448bf2c83de7cdee34ebabcf3de62f51cda\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe SubagentStop hook (task_status_hook.py) does not fire when agents are launched via the Agent tool during /implement-feature. Tasks remain in-progress after agent completion. The orchestrator must manually call sam_state to mark tasks complete. Observed across multiple task plans in session 2026-03-21: T01-T03 for issue 919, T01-T09 for issue 920, T1 for issue 927, T01-T04 for issue 938.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-21T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **subagentstop hook does not mark sam tasks complete when agents launched via agent tool** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-21T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-03-21 milestone orchestration implementation\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Tasks remain stuck in-progress after agent completion, forcing manual orchestrator intervention across every implement-feature session. Observed across 17 tasks in a single day (2026-03-21). Breaks the automated SAM completion pipeline.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Every /implement-feature session that uses parallel Agent tool dispatch (TeamCreate). All T0x tasks in plans 919, 920, 927, 938 were affected.\\n- Bottleneck: Orchestrator must poll sam_state manually after each agent completes, turning an automated hook into a manual step.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Restores zero-touch task completion: sub-agent finishes \u2192 task auto-marked COMPLETE, no orchestrator intervention.\\n- Enables accurate SAM progress tracking during parallel agent dispatch.\\n- Removes a recurring manual workaround that causes timestamp inconsistency and plan drift.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen any sub-agent launched via the Agent tool during /implement-feature completes, the SubagentStop hook fires in the orchestrator session. The hook reads `agent_transcript_path` from its input, extracts the sub-agent session ID from the JSONL transcript, looks up `active-task-{session_id}.json`, and calls `sam_update_status` to mark the task COMPLETE with a `completed` timestamp. The orchestrator observes the task as COMPLETE on next `sam_status` poll without manual intervention.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe SubagentStop hook fires reliably for every sub-agent spawned by the Agent tool during /implement-feature. The hook script receives a valid `agent_transcript_path` in its stdin input. The context file `active-task-{session_id}.json` exists at the expected path when the hook fires. The `sam_update_status` call succeeds and the task transitions to COMPLETE.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After any sub-agent launched via Agent tool during /implement-feature exits, `sam_status` shows the corresponding task as `complete` without manual `sam_state` invocation.\\n2. A `completed` ISO timestamp is present in the task section after hook fires.\\n3. Hook stderr emits `[hook] SubagentStop: no context file for session ... \u2014 not a /start-task agent` only for agents that genuinely did not invoke /start-task; it does not emit this for legitimate task agents.\\n4. The `agent_transcript_path` field is present in the SubagentStop hook input when agents are launched via the Agent tool (verified by adding a debug log to the hook).\\n5. When `agent_transcript_path` is absent or the transcript contains no parseable session_id, the hook exits 0 cleanly (no error).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py |\\n| Hook registration | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md (frontmatter `hooks:` key) |\\n| Context file writer | plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md |\\n| Hook registration (plugin-level) | plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json (does NOT register SubagentStop \u2014 only TaskCompleted, Stop, SessionEnd) |\\n| Reference | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-guide/references/inline-agent-hooks.md (plugin agent hook restriction, line 181-183) |\\n| Related bug | #339 \u2014 Orchestrator manually edited task status instead of investigating hook failure |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: #576 (SubagentStop hook should capture structured summary of subagent work) \u2014 that feature requires the hook to fire reliably first.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall to Medium \u2014 The fix depends on root cause.\\n- If Candidate A (hook not registered): register SubagentStop in `hooks/hooks.json` (the plugin-level hooks file) instead of/in addition to SKILL.md frontmatter. Small.\\n- If Candidate B (missing transcript path): add a fallback in `handle_subagent_stop` that glob-searches `active-task-*.json` files for any in-progress task when transcript-based lookup fails. Medium.\\n- Diagnostic run to confirm root cause: Small (add 3 lines of stderr logging, run one /implement-feature session, inspect output).\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Root cause is unconfirmed: two candidate explanations exist (see below); a diagnostic run is needed to determine which applies.\\n  - Candidate A: The `hooks:` key in SKILL.md frontmatter is not honored for skills loaded into a session (as opposed to agents defined in `agents/`). Plugin agents have their `hooks` field silently stripped per official docs (inline-agent-hooks.md line 181-183); the same may apply to skills or the frontmatter hooks key in SKILL.md may not propagate to AgentStop events at all when the skill is loaded by an orchestrator rather than running as the subagent itself.\\n  - Candidate B: The hook fires but `agent_transcript_path` is absent or empty in the SubagentStop hook input for Agent-tool-launched agents, causing `_resolve_context_file_from_transcript` to exit 0 at line 547 without finding the context file.\\n- Verification step needed: add stderr logging to `handle_subagent_stop` to capture full hook_input keys and `agent_transcript_path` value in a live session.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `sam_status` output shows task stuck at `in-progress` after sub-agent exit.\\n- No `completed` timestamp in the task YAML/MD section.\\n- Session 2026-03-21: T01-T03 (issue 919), T01-T09 (issue 920), T1 (issue 927), T01-T04 (issue 938) all required manual `sam_state` calls.\\n- Hook stderr logs (if captured) would show either no invocation or a failed lookup in `_resolve_context_file_from_transcript`.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Create a SAM task plan with at least one task in NOT_STARTED or IN_PROGRESS state.\\n2. Run /implement-feature on the plan.\\n3. The skill launches a sub-agent via `Agent(subagent_type=..., prompt=...)` (the Agent tool, not Skill tool). The sub-agent invokes /start-task to write `active-task-{session_id}.json`.\\n4. Sub-agent completes its work and exits.\\n5. Query task status: `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_status(plan=\\\"P{N}\\\")`.\\n6. Observe: task remains IN_PROGRESS instead of transitioning to COMPLETE.\\n\",\"digest\":\"6776334ed77757c3886d3080821499e1de2fd45f8ec56e109afa142a99133d1d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgyOHA\"}"}